# `MLIR_SYS_220_PREFIX`/`TABLEGEN_220_PREFIX` -- `mlir-sys`'s own build
# script (plus `tblgen-rs`'s and `cleave-mlir-shim`'s) need these pointing
# at a real, installed LLVM 22 + MLIR (+ openmp, for this project's own
# OpenMP parallelization stage, `cleave/src/pipeline.rs`) toolchain.
#
# Run `scripts/setup-toolchain.ps1` from the repo root instead of setting
# these by hand -- it downloads/caches the prebuilt toolchain
# `cleave-llvm-redist` publishes (`doc/building.md`'s own "fast path") and
# writes the *real* `.cargo/config.toml` (gitignored, machine-specific --
# this file is only the tracked template/explanation) with the right path
# automatically. Already have your own LLVM/MLIR build (`doc/building.md`'s
# from-source fallback, or any other install)? `scripts/setup-toolchain.ps1
# -ExistingPrefix C:\your\install` points at it directly, no download.
#
# This file itself used to hardcode a machine-specific absolute path
# (`I:/Dev/llvm-mlir-22`), which broke on every other machine, CI included,
# the moment anyone else tried to build this repo -- that's exactly what
# moving the real values into a gitignored, generated file now avoids. If
# you'd rather set these some other way (a shell profile, a CI workflow's
# own env step) instead of running the script, that still works fine --
# these are the two variables that matter, `220` is the fixed "LLVM major
# version 22, no minor" naming convention `mlir-sys`/`tblgen-rs` use, not
# configurable to a different number:
#
# [env]
# MLIR_SYS_220_PREFIX = "C:/path/to/llvm-mlir-22"
# TABLEGEN_220_PREFIX = "C:/path/to/llvm-mlir-22"
